    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d573">

                <pb facs="0899" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.61/289a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Japan (Grew)</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-10-20T18:00:00-05:00">October 20, 1933—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. For your information, the President made public this afternoon an exchange of
                    messages between himself and the President of the All Union Executive Committee,
                    Moscow, in consequence of which it is to be expected that the Russian Government
                    will send to Washington <pb facs="0900" n="796" xml:id="pg796"/> Litvinoff,
                    Commissar for Foreign Affairs, to discuss questions outstanding between the two
                    countries. In commenting briefly to press correspondents upon this action, the
                    President explained that this step does not constitute recognition.</p>
                <p>Text is being sent by naval radio to Peiping for relay to you.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
